      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5e64041b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5f605d39.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5f65c461.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5f674f0f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5f780c96.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5f7f073c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5f83d4d7.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae2f5f868b77.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Mod:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Like a couple of other mods, this removes the check for Link's disguise to enter Gerudo Town after Vah Naboris. However, the effect  only takes place after talking to Riju when finishing the quest, at which point she gives permission for Link to enter town, and the dialogue of &lt;b&gt;ALL&lt;/b&gt; NPC's in town will adapt to whether or not Link is disguised, so no more calling Link a vai when he's clearly not.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;</description>
