      <pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:57:59 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/662701161cce8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a3290f3c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a102f8e1.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a2f0b32a.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a1d614c5.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a2aeffd8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a2209bef.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a25c1a04.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a1adb932.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a27bedd8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a1e32482.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a15c7168.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a30658cb.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a30bf383.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a2939d05.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a1ccbd95.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a316e553.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/663934b988b03.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6625c39a1be22.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6625c399ed2e4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a29b8777.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a1d94725.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a328d496.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a20ca68b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a30a7f2b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a29e53d7.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a03ca05c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a0cbf768.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a049129c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a2f2a7d4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66355e5360ab6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66355e538e442.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66355e5495b6e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66355e53a8083.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/663569cc5051f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/663569cc54832.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/663569cbb6194.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/664a9f15c0e8b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/664a9f161d6e2.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/664a9ec1b737e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a076b100.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/66259a08f4022.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6629792032f69.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/663aa540edc00.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/664a92d93875b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; UKMM Brighter Lights Darker Nights Cloud Fix&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bugfix&lt;/em&gt;: This will correct the odd clouds UKMM users experience in game when choosing the Brighter Lights Darker Nights option during installation of the QoL NG+ main file. Make sure it has priority over the other QoL files in your load order.&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;What?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;Quality of Life - New Game Plus is a number of independent options inspired largely by other major overhauls (&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49532"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hyrule Rebalance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/414822"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Relics of the Past&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49790"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Survival of the Wild&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/projects/35468"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Second Wind&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, etc) and presented in a way that is meant to maximize compatibility with other mods while preserving the immersion of the Breath of the Wild base game. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Originally these changes were adapted to work in tandem with the series of &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/335782"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Link&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/326426"&gt;Zelda&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;/&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/427992"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Linkle 3.0 Upgradeable Armor Rebalance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt; mods for a more expansive overhaul and though I recommend using the UAR mods, its entirely unnecessary to do so.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Some people may decide to only use one or two of these tweaks but when used together the mods in this compilation create a subtle but substantial lift to some of the games key features, making the environment more challenging and enemies more dangerous but giving the player some added leverage in the form of passive buffs, purchasable weapons, and more sensible armor effects and set bonuses.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;These changes are an alternative to other more far reaching rebalances such as those mentioned above and while some of the modules may couple just fine, most are either already present in those mods or may cause some conflicts to arise. Please use your own discretion when choosing which options to use with your load order and consult the &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quality of Life Readme&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; that can be downloaded here or found inside your Merged Files folder after installation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Why?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;I really like the feel of the base game and respect the mechanics that Nintendo choose and although I like the idea of what some of the extensive overhauls/rebalances do I feel that they change a little too much. I found myself trying to make patches for some of those mods but that wasn't always an easy thing to do.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Earlier this year I started studying other mods and talking with their authors and found that a large number of my favorite features are actually brought about by relatively minor tweaks and changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I was fortunate enough to get permission to study and use some of the assets for changes that weren't so easy, such as the AI used in the RotP Guardians, the RotP Champion Weapons, and the event changes for Better Inn Perks from Hyrule Rebalance. Some tweaks were recreated altogether and improved, like Portable Barbecue.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Features&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Beedle &amp; Kilton Arms Dealers (Beedle and Kilton sell weapons while Kilton has a selection of monster parts to trade for and all Traveling Merchants have a more robust inventory - making hunting them down worth while).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Alternate Town Shops (All town and village shops with on-display items have received a face lift and NPC dialogue has been changed to match the new items when appropriate) .&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Deadly Guardians (&lt;span class="fontstyle0"&gt;Aggressive, resilient, unforgiving, relentless, and more perceptive.&lt;/span&gt; These Guardians share their DNA with the RotP Guardians, they will **** your face and dance on your corpse. It's great!).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Delayed Master Sword (Similar to "Korok Trials Before Master Sword" except this version allows you to pull the sword with as few as 3 hearts once the trials are complete).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Weapons can be crafted at anvils (Another Life Expansion).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Improved Breakables (Inspired by Hyrule Rebalance where pots will drop ONLY rupees and boxes and crates have a MUCH larger variety of items).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Rupees and possibly even Rupee Rabbits can be found by cutting grass.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Larger Creatures (1.5x bigger).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Severe Environment (More damage from fire/ice/drowning/falling/etc).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Increased Swim/Climb Speed (Moderate buff to swim and climb speed to compliment a more severe environment).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Better Inn Perks (More stamina and extra hearts from inns).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;RotP Champion Weapons (Badass elemental champion weapons).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Master Sword (Master Sword will benifit from the "Ancient Prof" set bonus and has it beam damage increased from 20 to 100).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Early Master Cycle Zero rune placed in the chest in the tower of the Temple of Time.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Master Cycle Zero maneuverability similar to &lt;span class="fontstyle0"&gt;the changes made in Mad Master’d Motorcycle Mod&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="fontstyle0"&gt; (but less over powered).&lt;/span&gt; &#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Reduced Knockdown (Reduces the ability to knockdown/stunlock enemies).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Faster Enemy and Weapon Scaling (Pick up where you left off with end game enemies and upgraded weapons spawning immediately upon leaving the Great Plateau).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Upgradeable Armors (All non-upgradeable armor such as Monster Helmets, Tingle Armor, Royal Guard Armor, etc are now upgradeable).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;No Shield Surf Damage (This doesn't touch "surf friction" so the Radiant Shield will still be the fastest for surfing).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Portable Barbecue (Cook and camp anywhere!).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Option to turn off sleeping at campfires.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Updated version of Brighter Lights &amp; Darker Nights is included that has HGStone's sky texture fix added.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Treasure Hunt (Places rare items in hard to reach locations - see Quality of Life readme for details. &lt;i&gt;This has been moved to a separate mod in v1.0.3, the link can be found under Recommended Mods below&lt;/i&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Functional Lantern's (For darker nights users who keep getting stuck in Impa's house) that places three purchasable lanterns in the Giro NPC merchants inventory (see screenshots).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Patches, Patches, Patches (For various mods to help bring them into balance with the UAR series of Link/Linkle/Zelda mods).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Installation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;Using BCML install both &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quality of Life NG+&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; main file and &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quality of Life - Extras &amp; Patches&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. If you select the &lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Beedle &amp; Kilton Plus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt; or &lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Beedle &amp; Kilton Plus and Alt Shops&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt; options during the installation of the main file then you need to also install the &lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Quality of Life - Merchant Override&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt; patch which will ensure that BCML correctly merges and sorts the changes made to NPC merchant inventories with other mods that do the same.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I2m has released a fully portable version of BCML that makes life easier, &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/tools/23006"&gt;&lt;b&gt;BCML Unofficial Portable Edition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Merchant Override is meant to be installed as a .zip file so &lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;DO NOT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt; create a .bnp out of it. Place all of the Quality of Life files near the top (highest priority) in your mod manager and in the following order:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quality of Life - Merchant Override (Highest Priority)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quality of Life - Extras and Patches&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quality of Life NG+ (Lowest Priority)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;READ the tool tips, the words mean stuff!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src="https://files.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/664a92d93875b.jpg"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;PLEASE NOTE:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; After installation click on Dev Tools in BCML and select the View Merged Files option to open the merged mods folder. Inside you will find a folder named Quality of Life which will contain important information and special steps for preparing certain mods (Lurelin Dress, Linkle 3.0 Biker Outfit, Linkle Costume Standalone, etc). The images and information you find will depend on the options you chose during installation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;ALSO NOTE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt; If you install Brighter Lights and Darker Nights then you may want to use one of Silentverge's Survival of the Wild presets:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src="https://files.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/663aa540edc00.jpg"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Mods Included in QoL&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;The following mods are included or have similar patched or alternate versions in the Quality of Life installer. Take note of these mods and if you use the Quality of Life version(s) then make sure you disable the original/corresponding mod(s) from your load order.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/477369"&gt;Another Life Expansion&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1920307"&gt;Nebroc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/499219"&gt;Korok Trials Before Master Sword&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1920307"&gt;Nebroc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49788"&gt;Disable Fast Travel&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1680793"&gt;Silentverge&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49812"&gt;Early Master Cycle Zero&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1681024"&gt;Lye&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49782"&gt;Make Cooking Pots Instead of Campfires&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/289876"&gt;WiseHorror&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/299110"&gt;Kings Lantern as a Weapon&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1704241"&gt;Banan039&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/428419"&gt;Pink Guardian Sword and Shield&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1750563"&gt;i2m&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49535"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Wearable Lantern, Brighter Lights &amp; Darker Nights&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49535"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;by &lt;/b&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1680793"&gt;Silentverge&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/315391"&gt;Mad Master'd Motorcycle Mod&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1980774"&gt;Fruitymcdoo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/508557"&gt;RotP Champion Weapons Standalone&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/508547"&gt;QoL Alternate Shops&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/427992"&gt;Linkle 3.0 Upgradeable Armor Rebalance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/335782"&gt;Linkle 2.0 &amp; Link Upgradeable Armor Rebalance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/326426"&gt;Zelda’s Ballad Upgradeable Armor Rebalance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/431353"&gt;Linkle 3.0 Collection - Upgradeable Armor Patches&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/482346"&gt;&lt;b&gt;~Linkle Cottage Dress~ ALE Patch&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Recommended Mods&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://mega.nz/file/8N4WTBiS#AMcsci-xtYXv5Wetzg-1PEC_nzF3I0xJHqziv6IyxCQ" target="_blank"&gt;Amiibo Treasure Chests&lt;/a&gt; (Not hosted on GameBanana)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/439900"&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Legend of Linkle Dialogue Mod&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;b&gt; (For Linkle 2 and Linkle 3)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Compatibility&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;The &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shop and Merchant Redo&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; options are the primary concern, they make changes to the&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt; ShopGameDataInfo.sbyml&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/b&gt;file in the&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt; &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Bootup.pack&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; and BCML will not properly merge this file. Which ever mod has priority is the one that will work correctly. Luckily not many mods change the ShopGameDataInfo.sbyml file, the most notable exceptions being &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49532"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hyrule Rebalance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/414822"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Relics of the Past&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49790"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Survival of the Wild&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/projects/35468"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Second Wind&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. They will require a patch to work correctly with the Shop and Merchant Redo options.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For Second Wind, everything in QoL seems to work except for Shop and Merchant Redo, Delayed Master Sword, and Another Life Expansion. Just leave these options out when installing QoL.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;If you use UKMM and experience any &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;problems then report them on the &lt;a href="https://github.com/NiceneNerd/UKMM/issues" target="_blank"&gt;UKMM Github&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1 class="SelectedElement"&gt;Special Thanks&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span class="fontstyle0"&gt;Credit (and a huge thanks) to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="fontstyle0"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1698083"&gt;GingerAvalanche&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="fontstyle0"&gt;for going out of their way to create a tool that makes the creation of save flags for shops a (mostly) automated process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
